    {
      "id": "p00002",
      "text": "In consequence hereof, they had seized on a Biscayner, convicted of\nhaving married his godmother, and on two Portuguese, for rejecting the\nbacon which larded a chicken they were eating[7]; after dinner, they\ncame and secured Dr. Pangloss, and his disciple Candide, the one for\nspeaking his mind, the other for having listened with an air of\napprobation. They were conducted to separate apartments, extremely cold,\nas they were never incommoded by the sun. Eight days after they were\ndressed in _san-benitos_[8] and their heads ornamented with paper\nmitres. The mitre and _san-benito_ belonging to Candide were painted\nwith reversed flames and with devils that had neither tails nor claws;\nbut Pangloss's devils had claws and tails and the flames were upright.",
      "translation": "On avait en conséquence saisi un Biscayen convaincu d’avoir épousé sa\ncommère, et deux Portugais qui en mangeant un poulet en avaient arraché\nle lard: on vint lier après le dîner le docteur Pangloss et son\ndisciple Candide, l’un pour avoir parlé, et l’autre pour l’avoir écouté\navec un air d’approbation: tous deux furent menés séparément dans des\nappartements d’une extrême fraîcheur, dans lesquels on n’était jamais\nincommodé du soleil: huit jours après ils furent tous deux revêtus d’un\nsan-benito, et on orna leurs têtes de mitres de papier: la mitre et le\nsan-benito de Candide étaient peints de flammes renversées, et de\ndiables qui n’avaient ni queues ni griffes; mais les diables de\nPangloss portaient griffes et queues, et les flammes étaient droites.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00002",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00002",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
      "replacements": [],
      "sentences": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p00003",
      "text": "They marched in procession thus habited and heard a very pathetic\nsermon, followed by fine church music.",
      "translation": "Ils marchèrent en procession ainsi vêtus, et entendirent un sermon très\npathétique, suivi d’une belle musique en faux-bourdon.",
      "paragraph_id": "en-p00002",
      "target_paragraph_id": "fr-p00002",
      "languages": {
        "base": "en",
        "learning": "fr"
      },
      "replacements": [],
      "sentences": []
    },
